**Read:** [On-site nitrogen generators for food use — EIGA 194/24](../sources/Onsite-Nitrogen-Generators-EIGA.lingua#r_2VHG044YCF1X5GZRJVJJFN7NFH), the membrane system diagram and feed conditioning; the full membrane sections of the existing industrial separations course.

A module divides feed into permeate and retentate. At steady state F=P+R and Fzᵢ=Pyᵢ+Rxᵢ on a consistent molar basis. Stage cut P/F affects composition and recovery. These balances must hold even when a transport model is elaborate.

Cascades and recycle can recover valuable constituents or improve purity, while changing compression work and internal flows. A recycle can make equipment process much more gas than the net product amount suggests. Feed contamination can damage a membrane or alter performance independently of the nominal inlet composition used in a model.

**Work:** Close a hypothetical two-stage binary separation with one recycle. Check nonnegative streams and fractions summing to one. Explain why a favorable single-stage selectivity does not settle the system design. Compare a membrane and adsorption arrangement at the same delivery pressure, accepted composition, demand history and recovery boundary.

